;; rebuttal-presence — load-bearing claims exposed by an open rebuttal (REQ-KG-006).
;;
;; Booklogic port of assets/queries/defeasible/rebuttal-presence.rq:
;;   SELECT ?claim WHERE {
;;     ?claim a tbf:Claim ;
;;            tbf:loadBearing true ;
;;            tbf:supportsChapter ?chapter .
;;     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?cc tbf:rebuts ?claim ; tbf:ccStatus "addressed" . }
;;     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?claim tbf:axiom true . }
;;   }
;;
;; The :where binds load-bearing claims (load-bearing = true, the relational form
;; of tbf:loadBearing true) that support a chapter (joining the claim->chapter
;; coverage edge, the relational form of tbf:supportsChapter — only claims with a
;; supporting chapter qualify, matching the .rq). The two :not arms are the two
;; FILTER NOT EXISTS clauses, lowered to two independent safe Cozo negations on
;; the already-bound ?claim:
;;   - no ADDRESSED counter-claim rebuts the claim: a counter-claim row whose
;;     target-claim-id = ?claim AND cc-status = "addressed". Counter-claims are
;;     projected one row per cc carrying its LATEST status (P5.2 canonical:
;;     dedupe-to-latest-per-id), so this drops a claim whose rebuttal's CURRENT
;;     status is addressed; a claim whose rebuttal is open (including an addressed
;;     rebuttal later reopened) or has no rebuttal survives.
;;   - the claim is not an axiom (axiom = true): axioms are exempt from the
;;     rebuttal audit.
;; A load-bearing, non-axiom, chapter-supporting claim with no addressed rebuttal
;; surfaces -> it is exposed. bermuda's golden is empty: every such claim there
;; carries an addressed rebuttal.
(defquery :rebuttal-presence
  :find  [?claim]
  :where [[?c :claim/id ?claim]
          [?c :claim/load-bearing true]
          [?cc :claim-chapter/claim-id ?claim]
          [?cc :claim-chapter/chapter ?chapter]]
  :not   [[?r :counter-claim/target-claim-id ?claim]
          [?r :counter-claim/cc-status "addressed"]
          [?ax :claim/id ?claim]
          [?ax :claim/axiom true]])
